<title>USA: Maine lawmakers reject governor's health-care cuts.</title>
<headline>Maine lawmakers reject governor's health-care cuts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Maine state legislature's Health and Human Services Committee unanimously recommended that funding be restored for a whole host of programs.</p>
<p>The panel rejected Gov. Angus King's plan to cut funding for the state hospice council, AIDS education programs, elderly meals programs and legal services for the elderly.</p>
<p>The committee funded the programs with surplus dollars in the medicaid program.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
